    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d696">

                <pb facs="1275" n="1243" xml:id="pg1243"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.00/4–554: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Dillon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret<lb/>niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-05T20:00:00+01:00">April 5, 1954—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:26 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3729. Limit distribution. I delivered message Deptel 3482<anchor n="1" xml:id="d696-f1"/> to Bidault Monday evening.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d696-f2"/> He asked me to tell Secretary that he personally could
                    well understand position US Government and would pass on your answer to
                        Laniel.</p>
                <p>He asked me to say once more that unfortunately the time for formulating
                    coalitions has passed as the fate of Indochina will be decided in the next ten
                    days at Dien-Bien-Phu. As I left he said that even though French must fight
                    alone they would continue fighting and he prayed God they would be
                    successful.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dillon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
